# Trivy ignore list. CI fails on any fixable CRITICAL vulnerability
# (trivy image --severity CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed --exit-code 1); HIGH and
# above are reported as artifacts only.
#
# Policy for adding an entry:
#   1. Only for a finding that cannot be fixed in this repo (for example, a CVE
#      in the upstream circleci-runner binary or a base image that has no fixed
#      build yet). Fix it instead if a newer pinned version exists.
#   2. One CVE per line, with a comment giving the reason, the owner and an
#      expiry date, for example:
#        # circleci-runner 3.1.12 Go stdlib; fixed upstream in 3.1.13. Owner: @handle. Expires 2026-12-31
#        CVE-2026-00000 exp:2026-12-31
#   3. Remove the entry as soon as the fix ships. Trivy stops honouring an
#      entry after its exp: date, so CI fails again if nobody acts.
#
# The list is intentionally empty.
